{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLx8MEuQjPbXeqJGH2kg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I resolved the merge conflict and committed it as `bb6cd79`. Lint passes, typecheck passes, and the TS suite passes (6962 of 6962). No Go files are part of this merge, so I didn't re-run the Go tests.\n\nOnly `src/cli/review.ts` had conflicts. Each branch had changed the same review steps in a different way:\n\n- **This branch (ticket 22, snapshots):** pins the worktree before inference. It also wraps steps 10 through the end in a `try`/`finally` with a `durable` flag. That flag deletes the snapshot ref if the review exits before the run record is written, and keeps it after.\n- **The merged-in branch (ticket 21, verifier):** adds the verifier step after the finder. The finder result is now called `found`, the verified result `result:VerifiedResult`, and `partial` is also set when a finding comes back undecided.\n\nI kept the ticket-22 structure and put the ticket-21 verifier block inside the `try`, indented and rewrapped to stay under 80 columns. That means a verifier failure before the run record exists still deletes the ref. The verifier's tools and snippets use the same pinned tree as the finder.\n\nFor the header comment, I removed the outdated line saying verification is another ticket and kept \"Snapshot capture is injectable\". Git merged everything else on its own: the verifier imports, `verifierUser`, `lineRange`, the real gate-offer import, and the doc and ticket files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":158,"cache_read_input_tokens":71294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":158},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_i